<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baar, Switzerland</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baar is a municipality in the Swiss canton of Zug, north of the town of Zug. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was one of the three rural communes, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ageri">Ägeri</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menzingen">Menzingen</a>, that shared government of the canton with the town of Zug through a common assembly. It later grew into an industrial and residential town close to the city of Zug.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baar-switzerland.jpg" alt="Baar, Switzerland" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roland Zumbühl · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rathaus-Baar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
